    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.icons\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nSince pulling in the latest breaking commits my expected behavior around extension matching is broken. From reading the commit descriptions it doesn't seem like this is an expected change.\r\n\r\nI use an extension config to match `spec.ts` files in order to visually distinguish them from the raw `ts` files, in particular when using mini.files. \r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/64c69ba7-9782-4a08-bfcd-586e2e2b51cd)\r\n\r\nIf I revert to `d990e3d` then my expected and actual behavior match.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nNVIM v0.11.0-dev-487+gc025c049a\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua` (setup `mini.icons` with some `extension` override, e.g. `[\"spec.ts\"] = { hl = \"MiniIconsYellow}` ) \r\n2. `:=MiniIcons.get('file', '~/path/file.spec.ts')`\r\n3. `:=MiniIcons.get('file', '~/path/file.name.spec.ts')`\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\n`MiniIcons.get('file', '~/somepath/file.spec.ts')` == `MiniIcons.get('file', '~/somepath/file.name.spec.ts')`\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\n`MiniIcons.get('file', '~/somepath/file.spec.ts')` uses the configured hl from `extension` configuration.\r\n`MiniIcons.get('file', '~/somepath/file.name.spec.ts')` does NOT use the configured hl from `extension configuration. I believe it ends up using the filetype instead.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThe two outputs on `d990e3d`\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6b7691b2-4f09-44ed-8c65-a4e8a84f6aa1)\r\n\r\n\r\nThe two outputs on `842e51b` (latest)\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8f426402-dd5d-4dc9-b65b-e31d3457660d)\r\n",
