            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nThe icon data gets resolved as expected which unfortunately doesn't work out of the box for these (rather niche) cases. The reason is that 'name.spec.ts' extension gets itself resolved as 'ts'. This can be worked around with proper `config.use_file_extension`:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.icons').setup({\r\n  extension = {\r\n    ['spec.ts'] = { hl = 'MiniIconsYellow' },\r\n  },\r\n  use_file_extension = function(ext, _) return not vim.endswith(ext, '.spec.ts') end,\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nI'll take a look if there is something to be done for better out of the box experience, but at the moment I think the suggested approach is a reasonable tradeoff (considering what should be a rather infrequent occurrence).",
            "created_at": "2024-07-26T13:42:13Z",
