            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This proved to be a bigger problem which surfaced after recent changes. The issue here is that \"extension\" category itself doesn't resolve such cases:\r\n- `MiniIcons.get('extension', 'spec.ts')` with default config *will* return typescript icon because `vim.filetype.match()` will recognize it.\r\n- `MiniIcons.get('extension', 'name.spec.ts')` with config from this issue will also return typescript icon for the same reason. But arguably indeed should respect 'spec.ts' configuration.\r\n\r\nLet's keep this open for now. I'll see if this is reasonable to adjust.",
